        "# Theory\n",
        "\n",
        "## Introduction -  Practice"
      ],
      "id": "35e4ac19"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "from statsmodels.tsa.seasonal import seasonal_decompose\n",
        "\n",
        "import kagglehub\n",
        "path = kagglehub.dataset_download(\"arpitagupta11/superstore-csv\")\n",
        "path+\"/superstore.csv\""
      ],
      "id": "2b25e741",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df = pd.read_csv(path+\"/superstore.csv\", encoding='latin1', index_col=\"Order Date\", parse_dates=True)\n",
        "df.head()\n",
        "\n",
        "df = df[df['Category']=='Furniture'][['Sales', 'Profit']]\n",
        "df.head()"
      ],
      "id": "718a0b81",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df.dtypes\n",
        "df.describe()\n",
        "df.index"
      ],
      "id": "ddda9df3",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "dfg = df.groupby('Order Date').agg({\"Sales\":\"sum\", \"Profit\":\"sum\"})\n",
        "dfg.index\n",
        "\n",
        "dfg.sort_index()\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "dfg = dfg.resample('MS').sum() # month start\n",
        "dfg.head()"
      ],
      "id": "f7ae37bb",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 7))\n",
        "ax.plot(dfg.index, dfg.Sales, marker=\"o\", linestyle=\"-\", color=\"g\", label=\"Sales\")\n",
        "ax.plot(dfg.index, dfg.Profit, marker=\"o\", linestyle=\"-\", color=\"b\", label=\"Profit\")\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Sales and Profit Time Series\")\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"Date\")\n",
        "ax.legend()\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "48ceed1b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "flights = sns.load_dataset('flights')\n",
        "flights\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 7))\n",
        "ax.plot(flights.index, flights.passengers, color='b', label='passengers')\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"Passengers\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "result = seasonal_decompose(flights.passengers, model='multiplicative', period=12)\n",
        "fig, axs = plt.subplots(nrows=4, ncols=1, figsize=(12, 15))\n",
        "\n",
        "for ax, r, c, l in zip(\n",
        "  axs.flat,\n",
        "  [result.observed, result.trend, result.seasonal, result.resid],\n",
        "  ['b', 'g', 'r', 'black'],\n",
        "  ['Observed', 'Trend', 'Seasonal', 'Residuals']\n",
        "):\n",
        "\n",
        "  ax.plot(flights.index, r, color=c, label=l)\n",
        "  ax.set_ylabel(l)\n",
        "  ax.legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "c575098f",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Preprocessing\n",
        "\n",
        "### Missing values\n",
        "- mean\n",
        "- median\n",
        "- linear interpolation -> forward or backward fill\n",
        "- polynomial interpolation\n",
        "- seasonal decomposition\n",
        "\n",
        "### Outlier\n",
        "- statistical method -> z-score or IQR.\n",
        "- ml method -> isolation forest, DBSCAN.\n",
        "\n",
        "imputation or drop.\n"
      ],
      "id": "0c156735"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "from scipy.stats import zscore\n",
        "\n",
        "df = pd.read_csv(path+\"/superstore.csv\", encoding='latin1', index_col=\"Order Date\", parse_dates=True)\n",
        "df = df[df['Category']=='Furniture']['Profit']\n",
        "dfg = df.groupby('Order Date').sum().reset_index()\n",
        "dfg = dfg.sort_index()\n",
        "dfg.head()"
      ],
      "id": "d876da34",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "serie = dfg['Profit'][1:500]\n",
        "serie\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 7))\n",
        "ax.plot(serie.index, serie)\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Profit Time Series\")\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"Date\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"Profit\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "6aee6094",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Missing values"
      ],
      "id": "5de46317"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "serie.iloc[20:30] = np.nan\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 7))\n",
        "ax.plot(serie.index, serie)\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Profit Time Series with NAN\")\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"Date\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"Profit\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "16369822",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "serie = dfg['Profit'][1:500]\n",
        "serie.iloc[20:30] = np.nan\n",
        "filled = serie.ffill()\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 7))\n",
        "ax.plot(filled.index[:100], filled[:100], color='r', label='Filled')\n",
        "ax.plot(serie.index[:100], serie[:100], color='b', label='Missing values')\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Profit Time Series with NAN forward filled\")\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"Date\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"Profit\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "e1e661b9",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "serie = dfg['Profit'][1:500]\n",
        "serie.iloc[20:30] = np.nan\n",
        "filled = serie.fillna(np.mean(serie))\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 7))\n",
        "ax.plot(filled.index[:100], filled[:100], color='r', label='Filled')\n",
        "ax.plot(serie.index[:100], serie[:100], color='b', label='Missing values')\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Profit Time Series with NAN filled with mean\")\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"Date\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"Profit\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "4c139b59",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Outlier"
      ],
      "id": "f73720ed"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "z = np.abs(zscore(filled))\n",
        "outliers = (z > 3)\n",
        "\n",
        "cleaned = filled.copy()\n",
        "cleaned[outliers] = cleaned.rolling(window=5).mean()[outliers].astype('float32')\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 7))\n",
        "ax.plot(filled.index, filled, color='red', label='Original')\n",
        "ax.plot(cleaned.index, cleaned, color='blue', label='Outlier removed')\n",
        "ax.legend()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "0d646892",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Interpolation"
      ],
      "id": "4bf7609b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "serie = dfg['Profit'][1:500]\n",
        "serie.iloc[20:30] = np.nan\n",
        "filled = serie.interpolate(method='linear')\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 7))\n",
        "ax.plot(filled.index[:100], filled[:100], color='r', label='Filled')\n",
        "ax.plot(serie.index[:100], serie[:100], color='b', label='Missing values')\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Profit Time Series with NAN filled with mean\")\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"Date\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"Profit\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "0a047a08",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Exercise\n"
      ],
      "id": "54a06924"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "\n",
        "dj = sns.load_dataset('dowjones')\n",
        "dj.head()\n",
        "\n",
        "dj[\"Date\"] = pd.to_datetime(dj.Date)\n",
        "\n",
        "dj.Price.plot(title=\"Dow Jones\", figsize=(10, 7))\n",
        "# plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "0fcdff4b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# add missing values\n",
        "np.random.seed(42)\n",
        "missing_idx = np.random.choice(dj.index, size=20, replace=False)\n",
        "dj.loc[missing_idx, 'Price'] = np.nan\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
        "plt.plot(dj.Date, dj.Price, linewidth=2)\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "# add outliers\n",
        "outlier_idx = np.random.choice(dj.index, size=5, replace=False)\n",
        "dj.loc[outlier_idx, 'Price'] = dj.loc[outlier_idx, 'Price'] * 5\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
        "plt.plot(dj.Date, dj.Price, linewidth=2)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fae97906",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "dj.isna().sum()\n",
        "dj.info()\n",
        "dj.describe()\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(dj.Date, dj.Price)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "e374c363",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "sns.boxplot(dj.Price)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "6f36e148",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from scipy.stats import zscore\n",
        "\n",
        "dj['price'] = dj.Price.interpolate(method='linear')\n",
        "\n",
        "dj['rolling_mean'] = dj.price.rolling(12).mean().bfill()\n",
        "dj['rolling_median'] = dj.price.rolling(12).median().bfill()\n",
        "dj.head()"
      ],
      "id": "21a74dc0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "dj['residuals'] = dj.price - dj.rolling_mean # residuals = real - mean\n",
        "dj['zscore'] = zscore(dj.residuals.dropna())\n",
        "dj.head()\n",
        "\n",
        "dj.zscore.describe()\n",
        "\n",
        "outliers = dj[np.abs(dj.zscore) > 3]\n",
        "dj['price_clean'] = dj.price\n",
        "dj.loc[outliers.index, 'price_clean'] = dj.loc[outliers.index, 'rolling_median']"
      ],
      "id": "46a4208c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(15, 12))\n",
        "ax.plot(dj.Date, dj.price_clean)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "ce2f547f",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df = dj[['Date', 'price_clean']].rename(columns={'Date' : 'date', 'price_clean' : 'price'})\n",
        "df.head()\n",
        "df = df.set_index('date')\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "df['rolling_12'] = df.price.rolling(12).mean()\n",
        "df['rolling_24'] = df.price.rolling(24).mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, axs = plt.subplots(ncols=1, nrows=3, figsize=(12, 15))\n",
        "\n",
        "for ax, col in zip(axs.flat, ['price', 'rolling_12', 'rolling_24']):\n",
        "  ax.plot(df.index, df[col])\n",
        "  ax.set_title(f\"Time series {col}\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "d1f42a56",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(15, 12))\n",
        "ax.plot(df.index, df.price, label='price')\n",
        "ax.plot(df.index, df.rolling_12, label='rolling mean 12')\n",
        "ax.plot(df.index, df.rolling_24, label='rolling mean 24')\n",
        "ax.legend()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "61b68347",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "same concept using shif to lag data. \n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Stationarity\n",
        "\n",
        "Stationarity when statistical properties (mean, variance, autocorrelation) are constant during time.\n",
        "- *Low*\n",
        "\n",
        "  - $E[X_t] = \\mu,\\ \\forall t$ -> constant mean.\n",
        "\n",
        "  - $Var[X_t] = \\sigmaˆ2,\\ \\forall t$ -> constant var.\n",
        "  \n",
        "  - $Cov(X_t, X_{t+h}) = \\gamma (h),   \\forall t,\\ h$ -> autocovar depends only by h, the lag.\n",
        "\n",
        "- *Strong* -> join distribution $X_{t_1}, X_{t_2}, ... X_{t_n}$ invariant to traslation over time.\n",
        "\n",
        "Why it is so important?\n",
        "\n",
        "- *Predictive modelling*, for example with ARIMA, because this type of model assumes a stable data generation.\n",
        "\n",
        "- *Transformation techniques*, like differentiation, trend removal, log transformations.\n",
        "\n",
        "How to?\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Visualize data to understand if there is stationarity or not.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. Transformations:\n",
        "\n",
        "  - Diff.\n",
        "    \n",
        "    - Simple diff: $y'_t = y_t - t_{t-1}$ .\n",
        "    - Seasonal diff: $y'_t = y_t - y_{t-s}$\n",
        "\n",
        "  - BoxCox transformation.\n",
        "\n",
        "    $$\n",
        "    y(\\lambda) = \n",
        "    \\begin{cases}\n",
        "    \\frac{yˆ{\\lambda} - 1}{\\lambda},\\ if \\lambda \\neq 0;\\\\\n",
        "    \\log y,\\ if \\lambda = 0.\n",
        "    \\end{cases}\n",
        "    $$\n",
        "\n",
        "  - Detrend: estimate and removal of the series trend.\n",
        "\n",
        "3. Stationarety statistical test\n",
        "\n",
        "- *A*ugmented *D*ickey-*F*uller: $\\Delta Y_t = \\alpha + \\beta t + \\gamma Y_{t-1} + \\sum_{i=1}^{p} \\delta_i \\Delta Y_{t-i} + \\epsilon_t$, where reject $H_0$ : not stationary if p < 0.05.\n",
        "\n",
        "  - *K*wiatkowski-*P*hilips-*S*chidt-*S*hin: $Y_t = \\mu + r_t + \\epsilon_t$, where $r_t$ is a random walk.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Practice"
      ],
      "id": "24552c9b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "from statsmodels.tsa.stattools import adfuller\n",
        "from scipy import stats\n",
        "\n",
        "flights = sns.load_dataset('flights')\n",
        "flights\n",
        "df = flights['passengers'].copy()\n",
        "df.head()\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 10))\n",
        "ax.plot(df.index, df)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "df6c907b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "def make_adf(x):\n",
        "  \n",
        "  adf = adfuller(x)\n",
        "\n",
        "  print(f\"Statistic: {adf[0]}\")\n",
        "  print(f\"p-value: {adf[1]}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "  if adf[1] <= 0.05:\n",
        "    print('Stationary time series')\n",
        "  else:\n",
        "    print(\"Time sereis NOT stationary\")\n",
        "\n",
        "results = make_adf(df)"
      ],
      "id": "f08dc188",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "rolling_mean = df.rolling(12).mean()\n",
        "rolling_var = df.rolling(12).var()\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(ncols=1, nrows=2, figsize=(12, 10))\n",
        "ax[0].plot(rolling_mean, color='r', label='rolling mean')\n",
        "ax[1].plot(rolling_var, color='g', label='rolling var')\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "32af9923",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "transformed, lmbda = stats.boxcox(df)\n",
        "lmbda"
      ],
      "id": "19772a12",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "[!Note] The BoxCox transformation stabilize variance.\n"
      ],
      "id": "165a0b86"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "log_df = np.log(df) # a lambda close to 0 like 0.148 is similar to a log transformation\n",
        "\n",
        "log_df\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 10))\n",
        "ax.plot(log_df.index, log_df)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "2ea22023",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "diff_df = df.diff().dropna()\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 10))\n",
        "plt.plot(diff_df.index, diff_df)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "482950d3",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Lets check if the series is now stationary."
      ],
      "id": "e756e46e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "make_adf(diff_df)"
      ],
      "id": "05af8e77",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "It is not stationary, but we are very close. There is also seasonality."
      ],
      "id": "8c7a032a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "seas_diff_df = diff_df.diff(12).dropna() # differentiation at 12 period\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 10))\n",
        "plt.plot(seas_diff_df.index, seas_diff_df)\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "make_adf(seas_diff_df)"
      ],
      "id": "ea948149",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Doing this second diff to remove seasonality, we now have a stationary time series. It is time to create the final series with all the transformations."
      ],
      "id": "59df458d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "ts = flights.passengers\n",
