    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Forecasting\n",
        "\n",
        "## Classic model\n",
        "\n",
        "### AR model\n",
        "\n",
        "*A*uto  *R*egressive model *AR(p)*. It is a regression on itself.\n",
        "\n",
        "$y_t = c + \\sum_{i=1}^{p} \\theta y_{t-i} + \\epsilon_t$\n",
        "\n",
        "$\\theta$: autoregressive coeficcients.\n",
        "p: number of lagged elements.\n",
        "$\\epsilon_t$: causal error at time t.\n",
        "c: intercept.\n",
        "\n",
        "### MA model\n",
        "\n",
        "*M*oving *A*verage. Value at time t linearly dependent to previous forecasting errors.\n",
        "\n",
        "$y_t = c + \\sum_{i=1}^_{q} \\theta_{i}\\epsilon_{t-i}$\n",
        "\n",
        "$\\theta_i$: moving avg coefficients.\n",
        "q: n lagged elements for MA.\n",
        "$\\ epsilon_t$: causal errors at time t.\n",
        "c: intercept.\n",
        "\n",
        "### ACF and PACF\n",
        "\n",
        "The selection of the parameters p and q depends on this models.\n",
        "\n",
        "#### AR model\n",
        "\n",
        "- PACF: where data are 0.\n",
        "- ACF: decay to 0 esponentially or sinusoidally.\n",
        "\n",
        "#### MA model\n",
        "\n",
        "- ACF: where data are 0.\n",
        "- PACF: decay to 0 esponentially or sinusoidally.\n",
        "\n",
        "#### ARMA model\n",
        "\n",
        "- Both plots decay.\n",
        "- First lag on ACF depend on q from the MA model. After q, ACF decayment.\n",
        "- First p lag on PACF depend on AR model. After p, PACF decay.\n",
        "\n",
        "### ARIMA\n",
        "\n",
        "*A*uto *R*egressive *I*ntegrated *M*oving *A*verage. Useful for non stationary data. It adds differentiation.\n",
        "\n",
        "$y'_t = c + \\sum_{i=1}_{q} \\theta_i y'_{t-i} + \\epsilon_t$\n",
        "\n",
        "- p: order of the autoregressive componenet.\n",
        "- d: order of differentiation. Times of diff needed for stationarety.\n",
        "- q: order of the moving avg component.\n",
        "\n",
        "It uses ACF, PACF and also:\n",
        "\n",
        "#### AIC\n",
        "\n",
        "*A*kaike *I*nformation *C*riterion.\n",
        "\n",
        "$AIC = 2\\log(L) + 2(p + q + k + 1)$\n",
        "\n",
        "#### BIC\n",
        "\n",
        "*B*ayesian *I*nformation *C*riterion.\n",
        "\n",
        "$BIC = AIC + [\\log(T) - 2](p + q + k + 1)$\n",
        "\n",
        "### SARIMA\n",
        "\n",
        "*S*easonal ARIMA. It extend the ARIMA model to non stationary situations.\n",
        "\n",
        "SARIMA(p, q, d)(P, Q, D, s)\n",
        "\n",
        "- p, non seasonal component order.\n",
        "- P, seasonal component order.\n",
        "...\n",
        "- s, seaonality period.\n",
        "\n",
        "$(1 - \\theta B)(1 - \\Sigma B^4)(1 - B)( 1 - Bˆ4)y_t = (1 + \\Theta B)(1 + \\Theta Bˆ4)\\ epsilon_t$\n",
        "\n",
        "## Practice"
      ],
      "id": "84929f5a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "from statsmodels.graphics.tsaplots import plot_acf, plot_pacf\n",
        "from statsmodels.tsa.arima.model import ARIMA\n",
        "from statsmodels.tsa.statespace.sarimax import SARIMAX\n",
        "\n",
        "flights = sns.load_dataset('flights')\n",
        "df = flights['passengers']\n",
        "df.plot(title='Flihts time series', figsize=(10, 7))\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "e7e78748",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
